From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-macro: drop the LPASS core hw votes on runtime suspend

The rx, tx, va and wsa macro drivers take the "macro" and "dcodec"
clocks at probe and hold them until remove. On SM8750 those are not
clocks but q6prm hardware votes (LPASS_HW_MACRO_VOTE and
LPASS_HW_DCODEC_VOTE) that ask the ADSP to keep the LPASS core powered.
While any macro holds them the ADSP keeps its own RPMh votes, and the
AOP's low-power-mode monitor shows the AUDIO DRV as the only master
still voting through the whole of s2idle: cxsd/aosd/ddr never count,
DDR sits at 1555 MHz and the AYN Odin 3 drains ~1.9 %/h asleep. Android
on the same unit takes these votes only while a macro is in use.

Release both votes in runtime suspend, after the mclk/npl/fsgen clocks,
and reacquire them first thing in runtime resume before the register
cache is synced. Runtime suspend already marks the regmap cache-only, so
the LPASS core losing state while unvoted is covered by the existing
regcache_sync on resume.

diff -ru pa/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c pb/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
@@ -3976,6 +3976,8 @@
 	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->fsgen);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->npl);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->mclk);
+	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->dcodec);
+	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->macro);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -3985,10 +3987,22 @@
 	struct rx_macro *rx = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = clk_prepare_enable(rx->macro);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "unable to prepare macro\n");
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	ret = clk_prepare_enable(rx->dcodec);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "unable to prepare dcodec\n");
+		goto err_dcodec;
+	}
+
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(rx->mclk);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "unable to prepare mclk\n");
-		return ret;
+		goto err_mclk;
 	}
 
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(rx->npl);
@@ -4010,6 +4024,10 @@
 	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->npl);
 err_npl:
 	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->mclk);
+err_mclk:
+	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->dcodec);
+err_dcodec:
+	clk_disable_unprepare(rx->macro);
 
 	return ret;
 }
